| `secrets.scanner.release_assets.<platform>.file` | string | the v8.30.1 archive for each of `darwin-arm64`, `darwin-x86_64`, `linux-aarch64` and `linux-x86_64`, such as `gitleaks_8.30.1_linux_x64.tar.gz` | a bare `.tar.gz` file name, no `/`, `\` or leading `.`, under a lowercase `<system>-<machine>` key (Python's `platform.system()` and `platform.machine()`, such as `linux-x86_64`) | `scripts/install_scanner.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `secrets.scanner.release_assets` row | Names the release archive this platform installs, joined to `secrets.scanner.release_url`; its one regular member named `secrets.scanner.name` is the program. A platform with no entry is exit 14 before any fetch, naming the keys the map lists, and an archive without exactly one such member is exit 1 and installs nothing. Required with the whole map: absent, the installer is exit 14 naming `secrets.scanner.release_assets`. | where the archive is fetched from: `secrets.scanner.release_url` | always |
